    "trade": {
      "type": "content-columns",
      "settings": {
        "color_scheme": "ink",
        "layout": "list",
        "numbered": false,
        "eyebrow": "The trade",
        "heading": "Heavier than a racing sock. Lighter than a wet one.",
        "lede": "<p>A waterproof sock has three layers where a racing sock has one. There is no version of this where the weight is the same. The measured weight per pair is being confirmed and will be published here as a number, not an adjective.</p>",
        "mirror": true
      },
      "blocks": {
        "i1": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Bulk is the more real objection",
            "body": "<p>They sit at about the volume of a cushioned training sock. In a race-fit shoe with no room, that matters. In a normal training shoe, it does not.</p>"
          }
        },
        "i2": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "What you are trading it for",
            "body": "<p>A foot that is dry at mile ten in December rather than soaked at mile two. Whether that is worth three layers is a question only your local weather can answer.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "i1",
        "i2"
      ]
    },
    "whennot": {
      "type": "honest-limits",
      "settings": {
        "color_scheme": "ink",
        "anchor_id": "when-not",
        "eyebrow": "When not to",
        "heading": "Three runs where you should not wear these.",
        "cta_link": "#buy",
        "link_url": "/pages/technology",
        "lede": "<p>Every brand tells you when to wear their product. On a running page that is close to useless, because the conditions that suit a waterproof sock are narrower than the conditions people run in.</p>"
      },
      "blocks": {
        "w1": {
          "type": "limit",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Warm and wet",
            "body": "<p>Summer rain is the worst case. The air is already saturated, you are producing heat, and the membrane has nowhere to send the vapour. Wear a thin sock and accept wet feet.</p>",
            "width": "1",
            "tone": "wash"
          }
        },
        "w2": {
          "type": "limit",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Hard efforts in mild weather",
            "body": "<p>Intervals, tempo, anything above steady in double figures. You will out-produce the membrane inside twenty minutes and finish damp from the inside.</p>",
            "width": "1",
            "tone": "wash"
          }
        },
        "w3": {
          "type": "limit",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "A race-fit shoe with no volume",
            "body": "<p>If your racing shoe is already snug in a thin sock, do not put a three-layer sock in it. This is a training and long-run product first.</p>",
            "width": "2",
            "tone": "blue"
          }
        },
        "w4": {
          "type": "limit",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "",
            "body": "<p>Cold and wet is where these earn their place. That is most of a British winter, but it is not July.</p>",
            "width": "4",
            "tone": "paper",
            "side_by_side": true
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "w1",
        "w2",
        "w3",
        "w4"
      ]
    },
    "winter": {
      "type": "content-columns",
      "settings": {
        "color_scheme": "paper",
        "layout": "cards",
        "numbered": false,
        "eyebrow": "Winter",
        "heading": "The runs these are actually for.",
        "lede": "<p>Not performance. Consistency — the training block staying intact through the months when it usually does not.</p>",
        "mirror": false
      },
      "blocks": {
        "i1": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Wet feet get cold fast",
            "body": "<p>A soaked foot in five degrees loses heat quickly, and cold toes are the reason a lot of winter long runs get cut short. Dry feet stay warm at temperatures where wet ones do not.</p>"
          }
        },
        "i2": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Trail, water crossings and standing water",
            "body": "<p>On a wet trail you stop choosing your line around the puddles, which is faster and considerably more enjoyable.</p>"
          }
        },
        "i3": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "The pair waiting for tomorrow",
            "body": "<p>They air dry rather than tumble dry, which takes longer. If you run four mornings a week in winter, you need more than one pair — that is the honest reason the two- and three-pair prices exist.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "i1",
        "i2",
        "i3"
      ]
    },
    "blisters": {
      "type": "content-columns",
      "settings": {
        "color_scheme": "wash",
        "layout": "steps",
        "numbered": false,
        "eyebrow": "Blisters",
        "heading": "Faster feet, the same three causes.",
        "lede": "<p>Running compresses the same blister problem walkers have into a much shorter time, which is why runners feel it more sharply.</p>",
        "mirror": false
      },
      "blocks": {
        "i1": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Wet skin is weaker skin",
            "body": "<p>Saturated skin resists friction far less well. Keeping the foot dry removes one of the three things a blister needs, and at running cadence that is the one that changes fastest.</p>"
          }
        },
        "i2": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Fit does the rest",
            "body": "<p>A sock that bunches at the toe will blister you at any moisture level. Take the larger band if you are between two, and check for rucking before you set off.</p>"
          }
        },
        "i3": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "We do not guarantee this",
            "body": "<p>Some brands offer a blister-free guarantee. We do not, because blistering depends on your shoe, your gait and your distance far more than on your sock.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "i1",
        "i2",
        "i3"
      ]
    }
